{"text": "Michael W. Rallings\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nTo secure the position of Director of Police Services for the Memphis\nPolice Department, Memphis, TN\n\n2016 to Present Memphis Police Department, Memphis, TN\n\nInterim Director of Police Services - Director\nAppointed to Interim Director on February 1, 2016. Effectively led and\nmanaged the men and women of the Memphis Police Department\nthrough some its most challenging times in recent history, from\ninvestigation of three fatal officer involved shootings, to the line of duty\ndeath investigation of veteran MPD Officer Verdell Smith. Despite\ndrastic reduction in staffing levels, used data driven methods and Blue\nCrush to continue crime reduction efforts by (\u2014) 6.73% month to date, (-)\n0.33% year to date, and (-) 35.42% over the (2006-2016) trend. Worked\nwith City of Memphis Human Resources to ensure promotional process\nwere well executed. Managed budget of over $250,000,000, staff of\n2013 commissioned police officers, and 352 civilians.\n\nWorked closely with Mayor Jim Strickland and his Senior Leadership\nTeam during successful contract negotiations and FY17 budget\nadoption. Communicates well with key community stake holders, media,\nyouth, clergy, and business community. Worked with the Tennessee\nBureau of Investigation to establish procedures for the investigation of\nfatal officer involved shootings. Works well with local, state, and federal\n\nlaw enforcement partners. Served on numerous boards and committees.\n\nMember of Joint Terrorism Task Force (JTTF). Maintained a Homicide\nBureau clearance rate of 80%, despite record rate of homicides.\n\nRestructured the MPD command staff after the retirement of four\nexperienced personnel. Restructured the Multi-Agency Gang Unit and\nOrganized Crime Unit to combat the rise in street level violent crime and\n\ngang activity. Dedicated to community policing and community outreach.\n\nSkilled in Policy and Procedure Development, Employee Relations,\nContract Negotiations, EEO and Labor Relations, Arbitrations,\nPurchasing, Human Resources, Employee Development, Safety,\nLeadership, Training, Management, Special Events, Crowd\nManagement, Emergency Operations, WMD, Anti-Terrorism,\nInvestigations, Home Land Security.\n\n2011- 2016 Memphis Police Department Memphis, TN\n\nDeputy Chief of Uniform Patrol District |\u2014 Deputy Chief\nCommanded Uniform Patrol District 1], April 22, 2011 \u2014 January 31, 2016.",
